In-Reply-To: <e474b3790709130428mc3f8a00i66525850fd795971@mail.gmail.com>
References: <Pine.GSO.4.60.0708022213410.25215@weber.sscnet.ucla.edu> <e474b3790708031114j2a0f2d93wab4aa4b3203da2fc@mail.gmail.com> <e474b3790708031116i10fe3db2qc8995dc4e1ca2a44@mail.gmail.com> <e474b3790708301849p6212b79eod05d07e93d866388@mail.gmail.com> <Pine.LNX.4.62.0709100933470.19161@wws-6qcbw21.Princeton.EDU> <e474b3790709110400w1d78dcfdl93eb913a2f5e4fee@mail.gmail.com> <Pine.LNX.4.62.0709111004500.22942@wws-6qcbw21.Princeton.EDU> <e474b3790709130428mc3f8a00i66525850fd795971@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.62.0709130746350.2608@wws-6qcbw21.Princeton.EDU>

There are two problems. "weight" should be "weights" (you need "s"), and 
also the variable name needs to have quotations. in your example, you need

> summary(zelig(y~x,data=X,model="ls",weights="weight1"))

rather than

> summary(zelig(y~x,data=X,model="ls",weight=weight1))

Hope this helps,
Kosuke

