From kimai-cTYGs6MY1n5VX4AG5UhMJw at public.gmane.org  Thu Sep 20 05:04:46 2007
From: kimai-cTYGs6MY1n5VX4AG5UhMJw at public.gmane.org (Kosuke Imai)
Date: Thu, 20 Sep 2007 01:04:46 -0400
Subject: Re: Weighted observations in bivariate probit
In-Reply-To: <46F1261C.7070409-3s7WtUTddSA@public.gmane.org>
References: <46F1261C.7070409@mit.edu>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.62.0709200102260.29500@wws-6qcbw21.Princeton.EDU>

Unfortunately, the bivariate probit model does not support sampling 
weights. My understanding is that the weights for glm and other models in 
R are used for the fitting process (in iterated weighted least squares) 
and are generally not the survey weights. There is a package called 
"survey" which has several regression models, but we haven't wrapped it 
yet.

Kosuke

